From: Trijal Saha <trijalsaha2012@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 14:45:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] libzip: include unistd.h unconditionally

The vendored libzip only pulls in <unistd.h> on Apple and Switch, so
close() is undeclared on every other POSIX target.  That was a warning
until GCC 14; GCC 15 compiles C as C23, where an implicit declaration
is an error:

    core/deps/libzip/zip_close.c:666:9: error: implicit declaration of
    function 'close'; did you mean 'pclose'?

zip_close.c is the only file in the vendored C tree that guards the
include this way - libretro-common guards it on _WIN32 and takes the
unistd.h branch everywhere else, and the vendored zlib's gz*.c (which
would have the same problem) is not in Makefile.common's source list.

--- a/core/deps/libzip/zip_close.c
+++ b/core/deps/libzip/zip_close.c
@@ -42,9 +42,7 @@
 
 #include "zipint.h"
 
-#if defined(__APPLE__) || defined(__SWITCH__)
 #include <unistd.h>
-#endif
 
 static int add_data(struct zip *, struct zip_source *, struct zip_dirent *,
 		    FILE *);
